                <pb facs="0690" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 865.117/129.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Page to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 13, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>368. Informed following American citizens, held for military service, ordered
                    released as born after father’s naturalization: Gasparo Gallo; Francesco Leone.
                    Alberto Tumolillo has already left Italy. Following three, now under arms, being
                    looked into and a decision will shortly follow: Leroy Barsotti; Ugo Da Prato;
                    Francesco Ghiloni.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
